  "interpretation": "The FA ESC2 member has a 0x44-byte pre-payload header. Field at header+0x34 is a stored payload length and field at +0x38 equals the additive byte sum of that payload in all three versions. +0x40 is an expanded-length candidate; tested standard codecs do not validate it. The header layout is similar in function, but not byte-offset-identical, to the GT-1 container. Cross-product identical bytes do not identify executable status or ISA.",
